help_title:      str = "Aether Lens Help";
first_run_title: str = "Welcome to Aether Lens";
first_run_a: str = "Lens runs models locally and keeps downloads explicit.\r\n\r\nDetected system memory: ";
first_run_unknown: str = "not available";
first_run_gib: str = " GiB";
first_run_b: str = "\r\nRecommended starting model: ";
first_run_c: str = " (download: ";
first_run_d: str = ")\r\nHardware mode: Full GPU\r\n\r\nFull GPU asks Aether Engine to select a discrete Vulkan adapter and size its pool automatically. System RAM is only a conservative model-size guide; it does not promise that a model fits GPU memory. If Full GPU cannot start on this PC, try Conservative GPU, then CPU reference from the Engine menu.\r\n\r\nLens will not download anything now. Select this recommendation? You can then review it and press Pull yourself.\r\n\r\nYes: select the recommendation\r\nNo: keep the default model";
first_run_selected: str = "First-run recommendation selected. Review the model, then press Pull to download.";
help_text:       str = "Aether Lens quick guide\r\n\r\nBackends\r\n- Ollama uses the Base URL field and your local/remote Ollama server.\r\n- Aether Engine uses its native /api/chat server, normally http://127.0.0.1:11435. Start it with: aether_engine.exe serve <model> 11435 gpu\r\n- OpenAI-compatible reads OPENAI_API_KEY from the Windows environment.\r\n- Anthropic reads ANTHROPIC_API_KEY from the Windows environment.\r\n\r\nAPI keys\r\nPowerShell, saved for future app launches:\r\nsetx ANTHROPIC_API_KEY \"your_key_here\"\r\nsetx OPENAI_API_KEY \"your_key_here\"\r\n\r\nPowerShell, current terminal only:\r\n$env:ANTHROPIC_API_KEY = \"your_key_here\"\r\n.\\showcase\\aether_lens\\bin\\aether_lens.exe\r\n\r\nRestart Lens after setx. Keys are never stored in aether_lens.cfg or saved chats.\r\n\r\nSpecialist\r\n- General, ANCL, Industrial, and Auto select the system-prompt route.\r\n- Auto currently uses the General route and is reserved for future brain/model routing.\r\n\r\nChats\r\n- Save quick-saves to chats\\<Chat name>.lens.\r\n- Save As chooses a new .lens file and updates Chat name.\r\n- Load opens recent chats, Browse, Open chats folder, Duplicate, Rename, and Delete.\r\n- Rename uses the current Chat name field as the new saved-chat name.\r\n- Export writes Markdown.\r\n\r\nAttachments\r\n- Add > Image attaches an image file.\r\n- Drag one PNG, JPG/JPEG, GIF, or WebP image from Explorer onto Lens to queue it locally; dropping never sends it automatically.\r\n- Add > Paste screenshot attaches a clipboard screenshot.\r\n- Ctrl+V in the composer also pastes a screenshot/image.\r\n- Click a queued image thumbnail to preview it larger before sending.\r\n- Add > Text/code file attaches .md, .ancl, or .txt inline with the next message.\r\n- Add > Folder snapshot attaches a bounded local folder context for the next message.\r\n- Add > Vision helper selects Auto, Moondream, First vision model, or Off for text-only Ollama models.\r\n- Vision-capable models are required for direct image understanding.\r\n\r\nLocal models\r\n- Refresh reloads models from the selected Ollama or Aether Engine server.\r\n- Library, Pull, and Delete currently manage Ollama models.\r\n- Use selects a listed model for chat.";
help_engine_text: str = "\r\n\r\nAether Engine automatic mode\r\n- Aether Engine is the default backend. Lens starts the local server automatically and stops only the process it owns.\r\n- Lens remembers the last backend, model, Engine controls, specialist, chat name, vision helper, and Pulse visibility across launches.\r\n- Pulse shows waiting/streaming/stopped/failed state, time to first token, elapsed time, live estimates, exact final tokens and context use, prompt/generation/load timing, throughput, stop reason, and recent reply speeds. The Pulse button hides or expands the detail panel.\r\n- Engine opens friendly checked controls for Full GPU, Conservative GPU, CPU, output constraints, sampling style, reasoning, reply length, speculation, and timing.\r\n- Aether Engine currently caps one reply at 512 generated tokens. Pulse reason length means the model reached that ceiling; the scrollable chat pane did not truncate it. Use Continue last answer for more.\r\n- Direct answer is the default and prevents Qwen3 from spending the entire reply budget inside a thinking block. Think before answering is opt-in and uses a 512-token ceiling.\r\n- Full GPU automatically prefers the discrete adapter and sizes its VRAM pool; no VRAM number is required for a 16 GB card.\r\n- ASCII means the ASCII character set, not English-only language generation. All languages / Unicode is the normal setting.\r\n- Library lists curated Aether-compatible public model tags. Select one, then press Pull to download and SHA-256 verify it. Refresh lists the local engine store; Use switches the served model.\r\n- Installed does not always mean runnable: shared stores can contain GGUF architectures intended for Ollama or a future Engine. Lens checks the native Forward status before Use or Send and blocks unsupported models without replacing the current working model.\r\n- Model info shows native parameter, quantization, size, architecture, context, and compatibility statistics.\r\n- Low-level GPU kernel escape hatches remain developer-only command-line flags.";
help_hf_text: str = "\r\n\r\nHugging Face cloud open models\r\n- Select Backend > Hugging Face (cloud). Lens fixes the endpoint to https://router.huggingface.co/v1. Press Library to browse the live text-chat model catalogue; select a row and press Use to choose it. Refresh reloads that catalogue. The :cheapest suffix asks Hugging Face to route to its lowest-cost available provider for that model.\r\n- Create a fine-grained Hugging Face token with Inference Providers permission, then run: setx HF_TOKEN \"hf_your_token\" and restart Lens. Never paste the token into Lens.\r\n- Before each Send, Lens names the exact host and model and explains that the message, prior transcript, attached text/code file, and any matched knowledge excerpts leave the computer. No content is added to the transcript until approval.\r\n- HF_TOKEN is read only from the Windows environment and is never saved in configuration or chats. Usage can consume Hugging Face credits.\r\n- The proof supports bounded .md, .txt, and .ancl text attachments inline. Images remain local-only; cloud models run remotely, so Pull and Delete remain unavailable for this profile.";
help_vision_text: str = "\r\n\r\nNative Engine vision\r\n- gemma4:e4b understands PNG pixels directly through Aether Engine; no Ollama or vision sidecar is required. Attach or paste a PNG and send normally.\r\n- With a text-only Engine model, Auto or First vision model uses an installed gemma4:e4b as a sequential helper, then restores the selected chat model. The helper answers the user's exact image question and Lens labels that result as authoritative pixel-grounded evidence.\r\n- A bounded evidence excerpt is shown in the transcript so the helper and final chat answer can be audited separately. Lens switches only a local Engine process it owns.\r\n- Moondream is an Ollama-only preference. Off disables helper routing but never disables direct gemma4:e4b vision.\r\n- Engine vision accepts one PNG per message today. JPEG, GIF, and WebP remain previewable but are not sent to the Engine. Oversized image/context requests are also kept preview-only.\r\n- The native vision tower currently runs on CPU and can take about one minute before the first reply token; Pulse shows reading image locally during that phase.";
help_knowledge_text: str = "\r\n\r\nLocal knowledge\r\n- Add > Knowledge indexes one supported text document or a folder into the portable knowledge\\ folder.\r\n- Retrieval is deterministic and offline: Lens selects up to three bounded lexical matches for each prompt. No embedding model or database is required.\r\n- The transcript says exactly which [K1]-[K3] passages were sent. Open cited passage reopens Lens's archived excerpt.\r\n- Use indexed sources has a checkmark and can be disabled without deleting the index. Show index lists original paths, copied bytes, caps, and storage.\r\n- Clear index removes only Lens's copied corpus and generated excerpts; original files are never changed.\r\n- V1 supports plain-text formats and caps one file at 256 KB, the corpus at 4 MB, and folder traversal at 96 files / depth 6.\r\n- Knowledge is read-only assistance. Lens does not edit, build, or run indexed projects.";
help_conversation_text: str = "\r\n\r\nConversation actions\r\n- Right-click the transcript to edit/resend the last user turn, regenerate with the currently selected model, continue, or delete the last assistant answer.\r\n- Edit is reversible: Lens places the old message in the composer and does not replace later turns until Send. Cancel staged edit keeps the composer text as a normal new draft. One-shot image/file/folder turns must be reattached.\r\n- Copy the last user, assistant, full exchange, or local Pulse metadata; the last assistant answer can also be saved as Markdown.\r\n- To branch safely, save the chat, type a new Chat name, then Load > Branch current to Chat name. Existing files are never overwritten and portable attachment links are preserved.";
help_arena_text: str = "\r\n\r\nModel Arena\r\n- Press the cyan ARENA button to open the Arena directly. Choose installed Model A and Model B from its Studio-style dark dropdown lists; the last valid pair is remembered.\r\n- The outlined Arena prompt field shows a gray Write your Arena prompt here cue while empty. Type one prompt and press RUN SHOWDOWN. Arena sends the same isolated prompt and Specialist route to both models sequentially, protecting normal GPU VRAM.\r\n- Answers and Pulse measurements appear side by side. Blind mode shuffles the answer sides and hides their identities until one left/right/tie vote is recorded; the visible A/B selectors do not reveal the shuffled side mapping.\r\n- Arena Options controls blind mode and the readable local TSV history under arena\\. History stores models, vote, prompt SHA-256, and measurements, not the prompt or full answers. It can be shown, opened, or cleared after confirmation.\r\n- Arena V1 compares two installed text models on one local backend. It deliberately excludes chat history, knowledge, and attachments so both contenders receive the same reproducible input.";
help_voice_text: str = "\r\n\r\nVoice transcription — still in development\r\n- Voice is intentionally hidden from the current Lens interface while we replace the legacy Windows SAPI recognizer with a more reliable solution.\r\n- The prior implementation remains in source for development testing only; it is not a supported release feature. No recorded audio is sent to a model.";
help_privacy_text: str = "\r\n\r\nPrivacy Proof\r\n- Proof > Show Privacy Proof creates a native read-only report without calling a model or network endpoint.\r\n- The report classifies the active endpoint as loopback or network/cloud, hashes the Aether Engine executable locally with SHA-256, identifies the selected model digest when locally inspectable, and lists queued/context disclosure.\r\n- It also lists the exact portable app, config, chats/assets, knowledge, Arena history, and model-store paths.\r\n- The Proof menu opens those locations and provides confirmed clearing for the current in-memory conversation, copied knowledge, generated artifact previews, and Arena preferences. Saved chats and attachment assets are never bulk-deleted silently.";
help_rich_text:   str = "\r\n\r\nRich answers and Document Canvas\r\n- Assistant Markdown is presented as headings, emphasis, inline code, code blocks, lists, tables, quotations, and safe links. Saved chats and exports remain portable plain text.\r\n- Add > Document Canvas offers Markdown, HTML, SVG, and CSV. The whole visible answer becomes editable source; one complete matching outer fence from a small model is removed.\r\n- Markdown previews in the Canvas. HTML/SVG Safe Preview applies the fail-closed sandbox. CSV validates quoted fields and consistent columns without rewriting the draft.\r\n- Canvas can edit, copy, and Save/Save As to a folder you choose. Nothing is written automatically. Right-click any existing answer and choose Open last answer in Document Canvas to open it as Markdown.\r\n- Right-click the transcript to Copy last answer, Copy/Save last code block, Preview a safe HTML/SVG artifact, or show/hide reasoning sections.\r\n- Web links always ask before opening.\r\n- Sent images/documents add portable Preview cards; click a queued text attachment for its read-only viewer.\r\n- Lens never compiles, runs, or edits projects. Those workflows belong to ANCL Pad and Aether Studio.\r\n\r\nFull guide\r\n- Help or F1 opens guide.html. This compact panel is the missing-guide fallback.";
